    {
      "dom_id": "question-211996",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $3x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nThe modulus equals $14$ in all statements, which suggests we'll need to use the first property.\n\nNotice that the coefficient of $x$ is $3,$ and $5\\cdot 3=15$ is one larger than the modulus. Therefore, we can reduce the coefficient of $x$ to unity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ 5\\cdot 3x & ≡5\\cdot 1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ 15x & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ x+14x & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ x+0x & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ x & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,14)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
