      "dom_id": "question-213066",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use the multiplicative property of congruences to compute the following residue.\n\n$94\\cdot 74\\text{ mod }8=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}94 & ≡11\\cdot 8+6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡11\\cdot 0+6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 74 & ≡9\\cdot 8+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡9\\cdot 0+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}94\\cdot 74 & ≡6\\cdot 2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡12\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡8+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n94\\cdot 74\\text{ mod }8=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
