      "dom_id": "question-213022",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use the multiplicative property of congruences to compute the following residue.\n\n$84\\cdot 102\\text{ mod }5=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84 & ≡16\\cdot 5+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡16\\cdot 0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\ 102 & ≡20\\cdot 5+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡20\\cdot 0+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84\\cdot 102 & ≡4\\cdot 2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡5+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n84\\cdot 102\\text{ mod }5=3.\n$$",
