      "dom_id": "question-213204",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use the multiplicative property of congruences to compute the following residue.\n\n$83\\cdot 96\\text{ mod }10=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}83 & ≡8\\cdot 10+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡8\\cdot 0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 96 & ≡9\\cdot 10+6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡9\\cdot 0+6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}83\\cdot 96 & ≡3\\cdot 6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡18\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡10+8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0+8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n83\\cdot 96\\text{ mod }10=8.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
