      "dom_id": "question-213181",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the last digit in the decimal expansion of ${13}^{13}?$",
      "worked_solution": "If $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$ and $c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ then the following properties hold:\n\n- $ac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- ${a}^{k}≡{b}^{k}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$ for any positive integer $k$\n\nTo find the last digit, we need to calculate the following residue:\n\n$$\n{13}^{13}\\text{ mod }10\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & ≡10+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the exponentiation property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{13}^{4} & ≡{3}^{4}\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡81\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡8\\cdot 10+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡8\\cdot 0+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we decompose ${13}^{13}$ into a product of smaller exponents. \n\n$$\n{13}^{13}={({13}^{4})}^{3}\\cdot 13\n$$\n\nBy applying the multiplicative and exponentiation properties, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{13}^{13} & ≡{({13}^{4})}^{3}\\cdot 13\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡(1)^{3}\\cdot 3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡1\\cdot 3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{13}^{13}\\text{ mod }10=3\n$$\n\nwhich means that the last digit of ${13}^{13}$ is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-213181\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">20.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"213181\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>What is the last digit in the decimal expansion of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"202\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3F\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>13</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup><mo>?</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 6:23 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
