"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-61\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-2261\" x=\"807\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-62\" x=\"1863\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-28\" x=\"2515\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<g transform=\"translate(2904,0)\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-6D\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-6F\" x=\"833\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-64\" x=\"1334\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-6E\" x=\"4961\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-29\" x=\"5562\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-27F9\" x=\"7229\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-6B\" x=\"10146\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-61\" x=\"10667\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-2261\" x=\"11474\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-6B\" x=\"12531\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-62\" x=\"13052\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-28\" x=\"13704\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<g transform=\"translate(14093,0)\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-6D\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-6F\" x=\"833\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-64\" x=\"1334\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-6B\" x=\"16150\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMATHI-6E\" x=\"16672\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-29\" x=\"17272\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let's prove the first property. The proof of the second property is similar.</p>\n<p>It's straightforward to prove the scalar multiplication property from the definition of congruence. First, note that we have the following chain of implications for <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"7.806ex\" height=\"2.509ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.671ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 3360.7 1080.4\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://w